1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,337
What's today's video about? It's about Toyosu Fish Market!

2
00:00:07,337 --> 00:00:08,837
Scene 1: Exploring Toyosu Market

3
00:00:08,837 --> 00:00:12,845
This is Toyosu Market.

4
00:00:12,868 --> 00:00:15,549
Wow, it's huge!

5
00:00:15,573 --> 00:00:20,940
Yes, it's a brand-new and clean market.

6
00:00:20,963 --> 00:00:24,412
Is it bigger than Tsukiji Market?

7
00:00:24,435 --> 00:00:28,040
Yes, it's much more spacious.

8
00:00:28,064 --> 00:00:31,064
There are so many people here!

9
00:00:31,087 --> 00:00:34,579
There are lots of foreign tourists too.

10
00:00:34,603 --> 00:00:38,769
What time does it open every day?

11
00:00:38,792 --> 00:00:41,792
It opens early in the morning.

12
00:00:41,815 --> 00:00:44,656
Where's the nearest station?

13
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:47,913
The station is right over there.

14
00:00:47,936 --> 00:00:50,203
That's really convenient!

15
00:00:50,226 --> 00:00:54,039
Yep, and it's covered, so it's fine even if it rains.

16
00:00:54,063 --> 00:00:57,129
Let's head inside quickly!

17
00:00:57,152 --> 00:00:59,921
Alright, let's go!

18
00:00:59,945 --> 00:01:03,220
I can smell the fish already!

19
00:01:03,244 --> 00:01:07,019
That's because there's so much fresh seafood here.

20
00:01:07,042 --> 00:01:10,609
I'm getting hungry.

21
00:01:10,632 --> 00:01:13,873
There are plenty of restaurants here.

22
00:01:13,897 --> 00:01:16,670
What should we eat?

23
00:01:16,693 --> 00:01:19,711
There are so many great places to choose from.

24
00:01:19,734 --> 00:01:22,201
Which one do you recommend?

25
00:01:22,224 --> 00:01:25,108
Let's find one together.

26
00:01:25,131 --> 00:01:27,990
There's a map over there.

27
00:01:28,014 --> 00:01:30,055
Let's check it out.

28
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:33,480
The restaurants are on the upper floor.

29
00:01:33,503 --> 00:01:35,936
There's an elevator right there.

30
00:01:35,959 --> 00:01:38,359
Let's take it.

31
00:01:38,382 --> 00:01:40,719
I'm so excited!

32
00:01:40,743 --> 00:01:43,950
Me too—let's hurry!

33
00:01:43,973 --> 00:01:52,982
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

34
00:01:52,982 --> 00:01:54,482
Scene 2: Waiting in Line at a Famous Sushi Spot

35
00:01:54,482 --> 00:01:57,616
How about this place?

36
00:01:57,639 --> 00:02:01,672
Wow, there's a long line!

37
00:02:01,695 --> 00:02:04,628
This is Sushi Dai.

38
00:02:04,651 --> 00:02:06,823
Sushi Dai?

39
00:02:06,847 --> 00:02:08,380
That's right.

40
00:02:08,403 --> 00:02:11,338
It's a really famous restaurant.

41
00:02:11,361 --> 00:02:14,495
Is it the most popular one?

42
00:02:14,518 --> 00:02:15,931
That's right.

43
00:02:15,954 --> 00:02:18,721
There's always a line here.

44
00:02:18,744 --> 00:02:21,912
Should we wait a little?

45
00:02:21,935 --> 00:02:23,102
That's right.

46
00:02:23,125 --> 00:02:24,892
Let's get in line.

47
00:02:24,915 --> 00:02:27,883
There's a menu outside.

48
00:02:27,906 --> 00:02:30,152
What looks good to you?

49
00:02:30,176 --> 00:02:33,309
I love tuna.

50
00:02:33,332 --> 00:02:35,819
That sounds great!

51
00:02:35,842 --> 00:02:38,776
They also have set menus.

52
00:02:38,799 --> 00:02:42,015
There are so many kinds of fish!

53
00:02:42,038 --> 00:02:44,805
What would you like to drink?

54
00:02:44,829 --> 00:02:47,767
I'll have some hot tea, please.

55
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:50,403
Same here.

56
00:02:50,427 --> 00:02:53,994
It's our turn next.

57
00:02:54,017 --> 00:02:57,217
This place is so clean and nice, isn't it?

58
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:00,019
You can see the chefs at work.

59
00:03:00,042 --> 00:03:02,976
They look so cool!

60
00:03:02,999 --> 00:03:05,765
Here comes the sushi!

61
00:03:05,788 --> 00:03:08,476
Wow, it looks beautiful!

62
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:10,367
Let's dig in!

63
00:03:10,390 --> 00:03:13,928
This is so delicious!

64
00:03:13,951 --> 00:03:16,518
The fish tastes so sweet.

65
00:03:16,541 --> 00:03:18,436
It really does!

66
00:03:18,459 --> 00:03:21,547
I'm so satisfied.

67
00:03:21,570 --> 00:03:28,675
You can find the link to review today's video in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without prior notice.

68
00:03:28,675 --> 00:03:30,175
Scene 3: How to Choose a Seafood Bowl

69
00:03:30,175 --> 00:03:34,142
There's something else I want to eat.

70
00:03:34,165 --> 00:03:35,532
What is it?

71
00:03:35,555 --> 00:03:38,521
A seafood bowl.

72
00:03:38,544 --> 00:03:41,979
But we just had sushi!

73
00:03:42,003 --> 00:03:44,836
I still want to try it.

74
00:03:44,859 --> 00:03:46,829
Alright, let's do it.

75
00:03:46,853 --> 00:03:50,301
Let's go to a place called Oedo.

76
00:03:50,324 --> 00:03:52,924
Is that place famous too?

77
00:03:52,947 --> 00:03:57,355
Yes, it's a well-known spot for seafood bowls.

78
00:03:57,379 --> 00:03:59,179
Here we are.

79
00:03:59,202 --> 00:04:02,235
There are so many options on the menu!

80
00:04:02,258 --> 00:04:04,458
What are you going to get?

81
00:04:04,481 --> 00:04:07,748
I'll have the salmon roe bowl.

82
00:04:07,771 --> 00:04:11,538
I'm going for the sea urchin and salmon roe bowl.

83
00:04:11,561 --> 00:04:13,961
That sounds luxurious!

84
00:04:13,984 --> 00:04:17,075
Yes, I can't wait!

85
00:04:17,098 --> 00:04:19,732
Oh, here it comes!

86
00:04:19,755 --> 00:04:23,488
Wow, the bowl is literally shining!

87
00:04:23,511 --> 00:04:26,198
Would you like some soy sauce?

88
00:04:26,222 --> 00:04:29,555
Yes, just a little.

89
00:04:29,578 --> 00:04:31,476
Let's dig in!

90
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:34,515
This is amazing too!

91
00:04:34,538 --> 00:04:37,835
The sea urchin is so sweet and melts in your mouth.

92
00:04:37,859 --> 00:04:41,025
The salmon roe has such a nice bounce to it.

93
00:04:41,048 --> 00:04:43,882
This is absolutely delicious!

94
00:04:43,905 --> 00:04:46,638
You can barely see the rice!

95
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:50,428
There's so much fish on top!

96
00:04:50,451 --> 00:04:52,984
This is such a luxurious moment.

97
00:04:53,007 --> 00:04:55,685
Oedo really hits the spot, doesn't it?

98
00:04:55,708 --> 00:04:59,566
Definitely. We have to come back!

99
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,090
Scene 4: Visiting the Tuna Auction

100
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:04,534
Let's go watch the tuna auction!

101
00:05:04,558 --> 00:05:07,047
Where can we see it?

102
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:10,204
There's a viewing tour available.

103
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:12,660
Is it far from here?

104
00:05:12,683 --> 00:05:15,776
No. We're close, though.

105
00:05:15,799 --> 00:05:19,092
There's so much tuna here!

106
00:05:19,116 --> 00:05:22,882
Yeah, they're really big.

107
00:05:22,905 --> 00:05:25,939
Is it cold inside the market?

108
00:05:25,962 --> 00:05:29,095
It's a little chilly.

109
00:05:29,118 --> 00:05:31,595
I brought a jacket.

110
00:05:31,619 --> 00:05:34,595
Good thinking.

111
00:05:34,618 --> 00:05:38,088
What are those people doing?

112
00:05:38,112 --> 00:05:42,151
They're setting the price for the tuna.

113
00:05:42,174 --> 00:05:45,648
I can't hear them very well.

114
00:05:45,672 --> 00:05:47,909
That's because of the glass.

115
00:05:47,932 --> 00:05:51,466
But it's really interesting.

116
00:05:51,489 --> 00:05:54,689
I'm glad we got to see this.

117
00:05:54,712 --> 00:05:57,846
What time does this usually start?

118
00:05:57,869 --> 00:06:01,044
Around 5:30 in the morning.

119
00:06:01,067 --> 00:06:03,712
That's so early!

120
00:06:03,735 --> 00:06:08,183
Yeah, we were a bit late.

121
00:06:08,206 --> 00:06:11,419
We only got to see a little.

122
00:06:11,443 --> 00:06:15,702
Right. Let's come back next time.

123
00:06:15,726 --> 00:06:18,759
We'll have to wake up early.

124
00:06:18,782 --> 00:06:20,749
Yeah, we will.

125
00:06:20,772 --> 00:06:24,539
But I got a feel for the market's atmosphere.

126
00:06:24,562 --> 00:06:28,328
Should we take a photo here?

127
00:06:28,351 --> 00:06:30,385
Yes, please.

128
00:06:30,408 --> 00:06:32,974
We got a great shot!

129
00:06:32,997 --> 00:06:35,131
Thank you.

130
00:06:35,153 --> 00:06:36,653
Scene 5: Choosing a Knife as a Souvenir

131
00:06:36,653 --> 00:06:39,654
Let's buy a souvenir.

132
00:06:39,678 --> 00:06:41,811
What looks good to you?

133
00:06:41,834 --> 00:06:44,853
There's a knife shop here.

134
00:06:44,877 --> 00:06:47,244
I'd love to check it out.

135
00:06:47,267 --> 00:06:49,279
Let's go.

136
00:06:49,302 --> 00:06:52,468
There are so many knives.

137
00:06:52,491 --> 00:06:55,091
They're so shiny!

138
00:06:55,114 --> 00:06:58,481
They look like they'd cut really well.

139
00:06:58,504 --> 00:07:01,271
These are professional-grade tools.

140
00:07:01,294 --> 00:07:04,694
I love cooking too.

141
00:07:04,717 --> 00:07:07,321
Should I buy one?

142
00:07:07,344 --> 00:07:10,230
How much do they cost?

143
00:07:10,253 --> 00:07:13,226
Around 10,000 yen.

144
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:16,384
That's a bit pricey.

145
00:07:16,407 --> 00:07:20,340
But they last a long time.

146
00:07:20,363 --> 00:07:21,963
Yeah, we will.

147
00:07:21,986 --> 00:07:26,353
You can even have a name engraved on the knife.

148
00:07:26,376 --> 00:07:29,242
That's amazing!

149
00:07:29,265 --> 00:07:32,465
It would make a great gift too.

150
00:07:32,488 --> 00:07:35,088
Maybe I'll buy one for my dad.

151
00:07:35,112 --> 00:07:38,201
He'd be thrilled!

152
00:07:38,225 --> 00:07:39,991
Excuse me.

153
00:07:40,014 --> 00:07:42,348
Could you show me this one?

154
00:07:42,371 --> 00:07:45,538
This is a really cool knife.

155
00:07:45,562 --> 00:07:48,496
I'll take this one.

156
00:07:48,519 --> 00:07:51,452
That was a great purchase, wasn't it?

157
00:07:51,475 --> 00:07:55,008
Yes, I'm so happy!

158
00:07:55,031 --> 00:07:57,764
I can't wait to use it!

159
00:07:57,787 --> 00:08:01,266
Yes, I'll do my best with cooking.

160
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:04,056
Please take good care of it.

161
00:08:04,079 --> 00:08:06,646
Of course I will.

162
00:08:06,669 --> 00:08:08,169
Scene 6: Marutake – The Famous Japanese Tamagoyaki Shop

163
00:08:08,169 --> 00:08:12,202
There's a sweet smell over there.

164
00:08:12,225 --> 00:08:14,643
That's Marutake.

165
00:08:14,667 --> 00:08:18,350
What kind of shop is Marutake?

166
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:21,574
It's a tamagoyaki (Japanese rolled omelet) shop.

167
00:08:21,598 --> 00:08:23,896
Is it a famous place?

168
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:27,453
Yes, it's very famous.

169
00:08:27,476 --> 00:08:30,365
Let's try one.

170
00:08:30,389 --> 00:08:32,789
It's on a skewer.

171
00:08:32,812 --> 00:08:35,045
Easy to eat, isn't it?

172
00:08:35,068 --> 00:08:38,268
Be careful, it's hot.

173
00:08:38,291 --> 00:08:40,324
Let's dig in!

174
00:08:40,347 --> 00:08:42,715
How does it taste?

175
00:08:42,739 --> 00:08:45,539
It's really sweet.

176
00:08:45,562 --> 00:08:48,330
It's like cake!

177
00:08:48,353 --> 00:08:51,156
Yes, it's so fluffy.

178
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,954
I can taste the dashi (broth) flavor.

179
00:08:53,977 --> 00:08:57,813
Japanese tamagoyaki is so delicious!

180
00:08:57,836 --> 00:09:00,609
Should we buy some as a souvenir?

181
00:09:00,632 --> 00:09:04,166
Yes, I'd like to get some for my family.

182
00:09:04,189 --> 00:09:06,407
Does it keep well?

183
00:09:06,430 --> 00:09:09,564
Let's ask the shop staff.

184
00:09:09,587 --> 00:09:13,244
They say it lasts three days in the fridge.

185
00:09:13,267 --> 00:09:15,701
Then that's fine.

186
00:09:15,725 --> 00:09:18,492
Let's get the large size.

187
00:09:18,515 --> 00:09:21,481
I hope they'll be happy.

188
00:09:21,504 --> 00:09:24,590
They'll definitely love it!

189
00:09:24,614 --> 00:09:28,663
Marutake's tamagoyaki is the best.

190
00:09:28,687 --> 00:09:31,654
Yes, I want to eat it again.

191
00:09:31,677 --> 00:09:34,643
There are other shops too.

192
00:09:34,666 --> 00:09:37,100
Let's check out a lot of places.

193
00:09:37,123 --> 00:09:38,623
Scene 7: Rest and Dango

194
00:09:38,623 --> 00:09:41,518
I'm a little tired.

195
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:44,633
Let's take a break somewhere.

196
00:09:44,657 --> 00:09:48,143
There's Misuke Dango!

197
00:09:48,166 --> 00:09:51,166
Misuke Dango?

198
00:09:51,189 --> 00:09:55,882
Yes, it's an old Japanese sweets shop.

199
00:09:55,906 --> 00:09:59,073
Is the dango good?

200
00:09:59,096 --> 00:10:03,029
Yes, it's really delicious.

201
00:10:03,052 --> 00:10:05,942
Can we have tea too?

202
00:10:05,965 --> 00:10:09,765
Yes, they have warm tea.

203
00:10:09,788 --> 00:10:12,222
Let's go inside.

204
00:10:12,245 --> 00:10:14,982
What are you going to get?

205
00:10:15,005 --> 00:10:18,973
I'll have the red bean dango.

206
00:10:18,996 --> 00:10:22,263
I'll go for the soy sauce dango.

207
00:10:22,286 --> 00:10:24,286
That sounds great!

208
00:10:24,309 --> 00:10:26,883
And tea, please.

209
00:10:26,907 --> 00:10:29,040
Let's dig in!

210
00:10:29,063 --> 00:10:32,238
These dumplings are so soft.

211
00:10:32,262 --> 00:10:36,195
The sweet red bean paste is delicious.

212
00:10:36,218 --> 00:10:40,307
They pair perfectly with tea.

213
00:10:40,331 --> 00:10:42,465
This is so comforting.

214
00:10:42,488 --> 00:10:45,904
Mosuke Dango is really popular.

215
00:10:45,928 --> 00:10:49,468
There are so many customers here!

216
00:10:49,491 --> 00:10:51,661
It really does!

217
00:10:51,685 --> 00:10:54,519
I feel so relaxed now.

218
00:10:54,542 --> 00:10:57,435
You can buy souvenirs here too.

219
00:10:57,459 --> 00:11:00,259
Let’s grab some later.

220
00:11:00,282 --> 00:11:04,057
Japanese wagashi are truly wonderful.

221
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:07,714
Yes, I love them too.

222
00:11:07,737 --> 00:11:11,633
Alright, shall we move on?

223
00:11:11,656 --> 00:11:14,825
Alright, let's go!

224
00:11:14,849 --> 00:11:16,349
Scene 8: A Seafood Fry Restaurant

225
00:11:16,349 --> 00:11:20,149
Can you still eat?

226
00:11:20,172 --> 00:11:22,985
Yes, I’m fine.

227
00:11:23,009 --> 00:11:25,575
Let’s go to Odaho.

228
00:11:25,598 --> 00:11:29,400
What kind of place is Odaho?

229
00:11:29,423 --> 00:11:32,504
It’s a fried seafood restaurant.

230
00:11:32,528 --> 00:11:35,202
Fried fish?

231
00:11:35,226 --> 00:11:39,712
Yes, their fried horse mackerel is famous.

232
00:11:39,735 --> 00:11:42,785
That sounds delicious!

233
00:11:42,809 --> 00:11:46,142
The restaurant is over there.

234
00:11:46,165 --> 00:11:48,578
Let’s check the menu.

235
00:11:48,602 --> 00:11:51,668
They have fried oysters too.

236
00:11:51,691 --> 00:11:55,825
I’ll go for the fried horse mackerel.

237
00:11:55,848 --> 00:11:59,081
I’ll have the fried oysters.

238
00:11:59,104 --> 00:12:02,039
Could I try a bite of yours?

239
00:12:02,062 --> 00:12:04,829
Sure, go ahead!

240
00:12:04,852 --> 00:12:07,485
Here comes our food!

241
00:12:07,508 --> 00:12:11,585
The fried horse mackerel is huge!

242
00:12:11,608 --> 00:12:14,382
It’s so crispy!

243
00:12:14,406 --> 00:12:17,773
And fluffy inside.

244
00:12:17,796 --> 00:12:20,629
Would you like some sauce?

245
00:12:20,652 --> 00:12:23,349
Yes, please.

246
00:12:23,372 --> 00:12:26,506
This goes so well with rice.

247
00:12:26,529 --> 00:12:30,507
The fried oysters are delicious too.

248
00:12:30,530 --> 00:12:32,786
Let me try one.

249
00:12:32,810 --> 00:12:34,624
How is it?

250
00:12:34,647 --> 00:12:37,681
It’s like the milk of the sea!

251
00:12:37,704 --> 00:12:41,564
Odaho is amazing.

252
00:12:41,587 --> 00:12:44,661
Fried fish is just the best.

253
00:12:44,684 --> 00:12:48,451
I’m so full now.

254
00:12:48,474 --> 00:12:50,907
That was a great meal.

255
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:52,430
Scene 9: The Scenic Rooftop View

256
00:12:52,430 --> 00:12:55,432
There’s a garden on the rooftop.

257
00:12:55,456 --> 00:12:57,590
Let’s go check it out.

258
00:12:57,612 --> 00:13:00,106
We’ll take the elevator up.

259
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:03,738
Wow, the sky is so vast!

260
00:13:03,761 --> 00:13:06,961
The view is incredible.

261
00:13:06,985 --> 00:13:09,725
You can see the ocean.

262
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:12,581
You can see the Rainbow Bridge too.

263
00:13:12,604 --> 00:13:16,138
Wow, it's beautiful.

264
00:13:16,161 --> 00:13:19,327
The breeze feels so nice.

265
00:13:19,350 --> 00:13:21,798
There's some grass here.

266
00:13:21,822 --> 00:13:24,755
Shall we take a little break?

267
00:13:24,778 --> 00:13:27,848
Yes, I'm tired from walking.

268
00:13:27,872 --> 00:13:30,562
Let's sit on this bench.

269
00:13:30,585 --> 00:13:33,785
It's so peaceful here.

270
00:13:33,808 --> 00:13:37,080
The market was so lively, wasn't it?

271
00:13:37,103 --> 00:13:41,318
Yeah, this place feels like a different world.

272
00:13:41,342 --> 00:13:43,878
The night view is beautiful too.

273
00:13:43,901 --> 00:13:46,468
Can we come here at night?

274
00:13:46,491 --> 00:13:49,470
Yes, it's open until nighttime.

275
00:13:49,494 --> 00:13:51,951
This would be a great spot for a date.

276
00:13:51,974 --> 00:13:54,008
Yeah, we will.

277
