Yes, I'm looking forward to it.

311
00:15:29,807 --> 00:15:32,641
Let's have fun in Odaiba too.

312
00:15:32,664 --> 00:15:36,037
Alright, let's get on the train.

313
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:38,627
Yes, here we go!

314
00:15:38,650 --> 00:15:41,820
Today was so much fun!

315
00:15:41,843 --> 00:15:44,176
Thank you very much.

316
00:15:53,835 --> 00:15:55,335
Scene 1: Exploring Toyosu Market

317
00:15:55,335 --> 00:15:59,603
Listening Test

318
00:15:59,603 --> 00:16:04,670
This is Toyosu Market.

319
00:16:04,670 --> 00:16:11,577
N1 は N2 です = N1 is N2
市場(しじょう) = market

320
00:16:11,601 --> 00:16:14,671
Listening Test

321
00:16:14,671 --> 00:16:18,243
Wow, it's huge!

322
00:16:18,243 --> 00:16:23,176
いA + ですね = It is [adjective], isn't it?
大(おお)きい [big] ↔ 小(ちい)さい [small]

323
00:16:23,199 --> 00:16:28,699
Listening Test

324
00:16:28,699 --> 00:16:35,286
Yes, it's a brand-new and clean market.

325
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:44,237
いAくて + なAな + N = [adjective] and [adjective] N
新(あたら)しい [new] ↔ 古(ふる)い [old]
きれい [clean / pretty] ↔ 汚(きたな)い [dirty]

326
00:16:44,261 --> 00:16:48,028
Listening Test

327
00:16:48,028 --> 00:16:52,461
Is it bigger than Tsukiji Market?

328
00:16:52,461 --> 00:16:58,536
N1 より N2 = N2 than N1

329
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:02,460
Listening Test

330
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:07,051
Yes, it's much more spacious.

331
00:17:07,051 --> 00:17:13,351
とても + いA = very [adjective]
広(ひろ)い [spacious / wide] ↔ 狭(せま)い [narrow]

332
00:17:13,374 --> 00:17:16,722
Listening Test

333
00:17:16,722 --> 00:17:20,656
There are so many people here!

334
00:17:20,656 --> 00:17:26,089
N が たくさん います = There are many [living things]
多(おお)い [many] ↔ 少(すく)ない [few]

335
00:17:26,112 --> 00:17:29,912
Listening Test

336
00:17:29,912 --> 00:17:34,388
There are lots of foreign tourists too.

337
00:17:34,388 --> 00:17:40,555
N も 多(おお)いです = There are also many N
旅行者(りょこうしゃ) [traveler / tourist] ≒ 観光客(かんこうきゃく) [tourist]

338
00:17:40,577 --> 00:17:44,959
Listening Test

339
00:17:44,959 --> 00:17:50,193
What time does it open every day?

340
00:17:50,193 --> 00:17:57,304
N から = from N / starting at N
開(あ)く [to open] ↔ 閉(し)まる [to close]

341
00:17:57,328 --> 00:18:00,674
Listening Test

342
00:18:00,674 --> 00:18:04,583
It opens early in the morning.

343
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:09,974
いAく = [adverbial form of i-adjective]
早(はや)い [early] ↔ 遅(おそ)い [late]

344
00:18:09,997 --> 00:18:13,230
Listening Test

345
00:18:13,230 --> 00:18:16,977
Where's the nearest station?

346
00:18:16,977 --> 00:18:22,132
どこに ありますか = Where is [inanimate object]?
駅(えき) = train station

347
00:18:22,156 --> 00:18:25,714
Listening Test

348
00:18:25,714 --> 00:18:29,886
The station is right over there.

349
00:18:29,886 --> 00:18:35,619
N は [場所(ばしょ)] です = N is [location]
すぐそこ = right there / very close

350
00:18:35,642 --> 00:18:38,342
Listening Test

351
00:18:38,342 --> 00:18:41,445
That's really convenient!

352
00:18:41,445 --> 00:18:45,752
なA + ですね = It is [adjective], isn't it?
便利(べんり) [convenient] ↔ 不便(ふべん) [inconvenient]

353
00:18:45,775 --> 00:18:49,875
Listening Test

354
00:18:49,875 --> 00:18:54,742
Yep, and it's covered, so it's fine even if it rains.

355
00:18:54,742 --> 00:19:01,375
N も 大丈夫(だいじょうぶ)です = N is also fine / okay
雨(あめ) = rain
大丈夫(だいじょうぶ) = all right / fine

356
00:19:01,398 --> 00:19:04,832
Listening Test

357
00:19:04,832 --> 00:19:08,826
Let's head inside quickly!

358
00:19:08,826 --> 00:19:14,326
Vましょう = Let's V
入(はい)る [to enter] ↔ 出(で)る [to exit]

359
00:19:14,349 --> 00:19:17,495
Listening Test

360
00:19:17,495 --> 00:19:21,161
Alright, let's go!

361
00:19:21,161 --> 00:19:26,228
Vましょう = Let's V
行(い)く [to go] ↔ 来(く)る [to come]

362
00:19:26,251 --> 00:19:29,884
Listening Test

363
00:19:29,884 --> 00:19:34,118
I can smell the fish already!

364
00:19:34,118 --> 00:19:39,951
N の においが します = smells like N
魚(さかな) = fish
におい = smell / odor

365
00:19:39,974 --> 00:19:44,041
Listening Test

366
00:19:44,041 --> 00:19:48,837
That's because there's so much fresh seafood here.

367
00:19:48,837 --> 00:19:55,395
から = because / since
新鮮(しんせん) = fresh

368
00:19:55,418 --> 00:19:59,285
Listening Test

369
00:19:59,285 --> 00:20:03,851
I'm getting hungry.

370
00:20:03,851 --> 00:20:10,118
お腹(なか)が すきました = I'm hungry
お腹(なか) = stomach

371
00:20:10,141 --> 00:20:13,713
Listening Test

372
00:20:13,713 --> 00:20:17,946
There are plenty of restaurants here.

373
00:20:17,946 --> 00:20:23,713
N が たくさん あります = There are many [inanimate objects]

374
00:20:23,736 --> 00:20:26,890
Listening Test

375
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:30,561
What should we eat?

376
00:20:30,561 --> 00:20:35,628
何(なに)を Vましょうか = What shall we V?
食(た)べる [to eat] ↔ 飲(の)む [to drink]

377
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:39,027
Listening Test

378
00:20:39,027 --> 00:20:42,984
There are so many great places to choose from.

379
00:20:42,984 --> 00:20:48,417
いA + N = [adjective] N
美味(おい)しい [delicious] ↔ まずい [bad-tasting]
お店(みせ) = shop / restaurant

380
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:51,310
Listening Test

381
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:54,643
Which one do you recommend?

382
00:20:54,643 --> 00:20:59,225
どこが いいですか = Where would be good? / Which one do you recommend?
いい [good] ↔ 悪(わる)い [bad]

383
00:20:59,249 --> 00:21:02,516
Listening Test

384
00:21:02,516 --> 00:21:06,301
Let's find one together.

385
00:21:06,301 --> 00:21:11,534
一緒(いっしょ)に Vましょう = Let's V together
一緒(いっしょ)に = together
探(さが)す = to search / look for

386
00:21:11,557 --> 00:21:14,790
Listening Test

387
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:18,547
There's a map over there.

388
00:21:18,547 --> 00:21:23,740
[場所(ばしょ)] に N が あります = There is N in/at [location]
マップ [map] ≒ 地図(ちず) [map]

389
00:21:23,763 --> 00:21:26,263
Listening Test

390
00:21:26,263 --> 00:21:29,130
Let's check it out.

391
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:33,111
Vて みましょう = Let's try to V
見(み)る = to look / watch

392
00:21:33,134 --> 00:21:36,852
Listening Test

393
00:21:36,852 --> 00:21:41,236
The restaurants are on the upper floor.

394
00:21:41,236 --> 00:21:47,269
N1 の N2 = N2 of N1
上(うえ) [up / above] ↔ 下(した) [down / below]
階(かい) = floor / story

395
00:21:47,292 --> 00:21:50,126
Listening Test

396
00:21:50,126 --> 00:21:53,426
There's an elevator right there.

397
00:21:53,426 --> 00:21:57,960
N が あります = There is N
エレベーター = elevator

398
00:21:57,983 --> 00:22:00,783
Listening Test

399
00:22:00,783 --> 00:22:04,049
Let's take it.

400
00:22:04,049 --> 00:22:08,549
N に 乗(の)りましょう = Let's get on / ride N
乗(の)る [to ride / get on] ↔ 降(お)りる [to get off]

401
00:22:08,572 --> 00:22:11,324
Listening Test

402
00:22:11,324 --> 00:22:14,492
I'm so excited!

403
00:22:14,492 --> 00:22:18,876
N ですね = It's N, isn't it?
楽(たの)しみ = fun / looking forward to it

404
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:22,452
Listening Test

405
00:22:22,452 --> 00:22:26,607
Me too—let's hurry!

406
00:22:26,607 --> 00:22:32,307
Vましょう = Let's V
急(いそ)ぐ = to hurry

407
00:22:32,331 --> 00:22:33,831
Scene 2: Waiting in Line at a Famous Sushi Spot

408
00:22:33,831 --> 00:22:37,298
Listening Test

409
00:22:37,298 --> 00:22:41,364
How about this place?

410
00:22:41,364 --> 00:22:46,943
N + はどうですか = How about N?
お店(みせ) = shop, restaurant

411
00:22:46,967 --> 00:22:51,241
Listening Test

412
00:22:51,241 --> 00:22:56,313
Wow, there's a long line!

413
00:22:56,313 --> 00:23:03,247
Vています = is / are V-ing
並(なら)ぶ = to line up

414
00:23:03,270 --> 00:23:06,548
Listening Test

415
00:23:06,548 --> 00:23:10,382
This is Sushi Dai.

416
00:23:10,382 --> 00:23:15,661
ここは + N + です = This is N
寿司(すし) = sushi

417
00:23:15,684 --> 00:23:18,317
Listening Test

418
00:23:18,317 --> 00:23:21,310
Sushi Dai?

419
00:23:21,310 --> 00:23:25,455
N + ですか = Is it N?

420
00:23:25,479 --> 00:23:27,512
That's right.

421
00:23:27,535 --> 00:23:30,835
Listening Test

422
00:23:30,835 --> 00:23:34,702
It's a really famous restaurant.

423
00:23:34,702 --> 00:23:40,002
なA + な + N = [na-adjective] N
有名(ゆうめい) [famous] ↔ 無名(むめい) [unknown]

424
00:23:40,025 --> 00:23:43,492
Listening Test

425
00:23:43,492 --> 00:23:47,558
Is it the most popular one?

426
00:23:47,558 --> 00:23:53,132
一番(いちばん) + N = the most N
人気(にんき) = popularity

427
00:23:53,156 --> 00:23:55,089
That's right.

428
00:23:55,112 --> 00:23:58,262
Listening Test

429
00:23:58,262 --> 00:24:01,932
There's always a line here.

430
00:24:01,932 --> 00:24:06,999
いつも + V = always V
行列(ぎょうれつ) = line, queue

431
00:24:07,022 --> 00:24:10,530
Listening Test

432
00:24:10,530 --> 00:24:14,650
Should we wait a little?

433
00:24:14,650 --> 00:24:20,317
Vましょうか = Shall we V?
少(すこ)し [a little] ↔ たくさん [a lot]
待(ま)つ = to wait

434
00:24:20,340 --> 00:24:22,040
That's right.

435
00:24:22,063 --> 00:24:24,329
Listening Test

436
00:24:24,329 --> 00:24:26,871
Let's get in line.

437
00:24:26,871 --> 00:24:30,406
Vましょう = Let's V
並(なら)ぶ = to line up

438
00:24:30,430 --> 00:24:33,763
Listening Test

439
00:24:33,763 --> 00:24:37,663
There's a menu outside.

440
00:24:37,663 --> 00:24:42,996
N + に + N + があります = There is N in/at N
外(そと) [outside] ↔ 中(なか) [inside]
メニュー = menu

441
00:24:43,019 --> 00:24:45,697
Listening Test

442
00:24:45,697 --> 00:24:48,797
What looks good to you?

443
00:24:48,797 --> 00:24:53,097
何(なに) + がいいですか = What would you like?

444
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:56,587
Listening Test

445
00:24:56,587 --> 00:25:00,627
I love tuna.

446
00:25:00,627 --> 00:25:06,184
N + が好(す)きです = like N
まぐろ = tuna
好(す)き [like] ↔ 嫌(きら)い [dislike]

447
00:25:06,208 --> 00:25:09,108
Listening Test

448
00:25:09,108 --> 00:25:12,455
That sounds great!

449
00:25:12,455 --> 00:25:17,088
いいですね = Sounds good!

450
00:25:17,111 --> 00:25:20,411
Listening Test

451
00:25:20,411 --> 00:25:24,245
They also have set menus.

452
00:25:24,245 --> 00:25:29,545
N + もあります = There is also N
セット = set menu, combo

453
00:25:29,568 --> 00:25:33,122
Listening Test

454
00:25:33,122 --> 00:25:37,295
There are so many kinds of fish!

455
00:25:37,295 --> 00:25:43,012
いろいろな + N = various N
色々(いろいろ)な = various
魚(さかな) = fish

456
00:25:43,035 --> 00:25:46,173
Listening Test

457
00:25:46,173 --> 00:25:49,840
What would you like to drink?

458
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:54,874
N + にします = I'll go with N
飲(の)み物(もの) [drink] ↔ 食(た)べ物(もの) [food]

459
00:25:54,897 --> 00:25:58,197
Listening Test

460
00:25:58,197 --> 00:26:02,064
I'll have some hot tea, please.

461
00:26:02,064 --> 00:26:07,397
N + をお願(ねが)いします = N, please
温(あたた)かい [warm] ↔ 冷(つめ)たい [cold]
お茶(ちゃ) = green tea, tea

462
00:26:07,420 --> 00:26:10,453
Listening Test

463
00:26:10,453 --> 00:26:13,953
Same here.

464
00:26:13,953 --> 00:26:18,787
N + も同(おな)じです = N is also the same
Same ↔ Different

465
00:26:18,810 --> 00:26:22,676
Listening Test

466
00:26:22,676 --> 00:26:27,229
It's our turn next.

467
00:26:27,229 --> 00:26:33,496
次(つぎ)は + N + です = Next is N
Next = next
Turn/Order = turn, order

468
00:26:33,519 --> 00:26:37,033
Listening Test

469
00:26:37,033 --> 00:26:41,166
This place is so clean and nice, isn't it?

470
00:26:41,166 --> 00:26:46,840
N + の中(なか) = inside N
Inside ↔ Outside
Clean/Beautiful ↔ Dirty

471
00:26:46,864 --> 00:26:50,020
Listening Test

472
00:26:50,020 --> 00:26:53,693
You can see the chefs at work.

473
00:26:53,693 --> 00:26:58,760
N + が見(み)えます = N is visible / You can see N
Craftsman/Chef = craftsman, chef
Visible = to be visible

474
00:26:58,783 --> 00:27:02,059
Listening Test

475
00:27:02,059 --> 00:27:05,892
They look so cool!

476
00:27:05,892 --> 00:27:11,159
とても + いA = very [i-adjective]
Cool ↔ Uncool

477
00:27:11,182 --> 00:27:14,318
Listening Test

478
00:27:14,318 --> 00:27:17,984
Here comes the sushi!

479
00:27:17,984 --> 00:27:23,018
Vました = V-ed (past tense)
Sushi = sushi
Come ↔ Go

480
00:27:23,041 --> 00:27:26,141
Listening Test

481
00:27:26,141 --> 00:27:29,712
Wow, it looks beautiful!

482
00:27:29,712 --> 00:27:34,645
なA + です = is [na-adjective]
Clean/Beautiful ↔ Dirty

483
00:27:34,668 --> 00:27:37,004
Listening Test

484
00:27:37,004 --> 00:27:39,671
Let's dig in!

485
00:27:39,671 --> 00:27:43,376
いただきます = Let’s eat! (said before meals)

486
00:27:43,399 --> 00:27:47,266
Listening Test

487
00:27:47,266 --> 00:27:51,811
This is so delicious!

488
00:27:51,811 --> 00:27:58,044
とても + いA = very [i-adjective]
Delicious ↔ Bad-tasting

489
00:27:58,067 --> 00:28:01,021
Listening Test

490
00:28:01,021 --> 00:28:04,454
The fish tastes so sweet.

491
00:28:04,454 --> 00:28:09,157
いA + ですね = It’s [i-adjective], isn’t it?
Sweet ↔ Spicy

492
00:28:09,181 --> 00:28:11,551
Listening Test

493
00:28:11,551 --> 00:28:14,251
It really does!

494
00:28:14,251 --> 00:28:17,989
本当(ほんとう)ですね = That’s true, isn’t it?
True/Real = truth, real

495
00:28:18,013 --> 00:28:21,479
Listening Test

496
00:28:21,479 --> 00:28:25,518
I'm so satisfied.

497
00:28:25,518 --> 00:28:31,056
とても / とっても + Vました = was very V-ed
Satisfaction = satisfaction
To be satisfied = to be satisfied

498
00:28:31,079 --> 00:28:32,579
Scene 3: How to Choose a Seafood Bowl

499
00:28:32,579 --> 00:28:36,779
Listening Test

500
00:28:36,779 --> 00:28:41,759
There's something else I want to eat.

501
00:28:41,759 --> 00:28:48,593
Vたい + N = N that (someone) wants to V
One more = one more / another

502
